Task prompt: You are building a system for handling various payment methods. Implement an abstract `PaymentProcessor` class and then create concrete implementations for `CreditCardProcessor` and `PayPalProcessor`. The base class should define the common `processPayment` method, ensuring all payment types follow a consistent interface.

Current code in the editor:
```
class PaymentProcessor {
  constructor(amount) {
    this.amount = amount;
  }

  processPayment() {
    // TODO: This method should be implemented by subclasses.
    // Throw an error if called directly on the abstract class.
  }
}

class CreditCardProcessor extends PaymentProcessor {
  constructor(amount, cardNumber) {
    super(amount);
    this.cardNumber = cardNumber;
  }

  processPayment() {
    // TODO: Implement credit card specific payment processing
    // Return a string like 'Processing credit card payment of $X for card ending in Y.'
  }
}

class PayPalProcessor extends PaymentProcessor {
  constructor(amount, email) {
    super(amount);
    this.email = email;
  }

  processPayment() {
    // TODO: Implement PayPal specific payment processing
    // Return a string like 'Processing PayPal payment of $X for account Z.'
  }
}

// Example usage (will be used for checks):
// const ccPayment = new CreditCardProcessor(100, '1234567890123456');
// console.log(ccPayment.processPayment());
// const ppPayment = new PayPalProcessor(50, 'user@example.com');
// console.log(ppPayment.processPayment());

```

